---
number: 569
title: One Sweetly Solemn Thought
author: Phoebe Cary
composer: Philip Phillips
tune: Philip Phillips
sp_category: "37"
topic: The Second Coming of Jesus
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
One sweetly solemn thought,
Comes to me o’er and o’er;
I’m nearer to my home today,
Than e’er I’ve been before.

[chorus]
Nearer my home,
Nearer my home;
Nearer my home today, today,
Than e’er I’ve been before.

[verse 2]
Nearer my Father’s house,
Where many mansions be;
Nearer the throne where Jesus reigns,
Nearer the crystal sea.

[chorus]
Nearer my home,
Nearer my home;
Nearer my home today, today,
Than e’er I’ve been before.

[verse 3]
Nearer my going home,
Laying my burdens down,
Leaving my cross of heavy grief,
Wearing my starry crown.

[chorus]
Nearer my home,
Nearer my home;
Nearer my home today, today,
Than e’er I’ve been before.
